WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.600
Tesla's roadster demo used 10 nozzles and 250 kilograms of compressed gas for the stunts. This

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:12.188
is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 636. Tesla ran the next generation roadster upside down on

00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:16.568
a curved ramp, through a mid-air flip and into a kickflip over a line-up that included

00:00:16.568 --> 00:00:22.168
the semi, according to electric. The thruster system can replenish its supply after recharging.

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:27.228
After the stream, Tesla detailed a performance configuration with active arrow and suction

00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:34.448
targeting under 1.6 seconds to 60. A thrust configuration with rear thrusters targeting under 0.9 seconds,

00:00:34.828 --> 00:00:39.708
and a rocket configuration with perimeter thrusters targeting under 0.59 seconds,

00:00:40.108 --> 00:00:45.328
and over 230 miles per hour. The car uses a yoke with steer-by-wire, fixed seats,

00:00:45.808 --> 00:00:50.688
and a mix of magnesium, titanium, and carbon fiber. Production is now targeted for

00:00:50.688 --> 00:00:57.508
28, and the Roadster page lists a range of over 300 miles across variants. Elon Musk warned

00:00:57.508 --> 00:01:01.868
during the live stream that success was not guaranteed given the experimental nature of the

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:07.874
propulsion. CyberCab's structural and assembly elements are showing up in the semi. Optimus

00:01:07.874 --> 00:01:13.414
actuators and mechanisms feed into the new Roadster Tessler-Roddy reports. Tesla is tying those

00:01:13.414 --> 00:01:19.194
programs together through common hardware in structural parts, actuators, and final assembly processes.

00:01:19.194 --> 00:01:24.834
The sharing holds even as each vehicle keeps distinct duty cycles and regulatory requirements.

00:01:26.001 --> 00:01:32.521
Annel White paint on the Roadster is formulated to handle ultraviolet light, cryogenic conditions, static and corrosion.

00:01:33.341 --> 00:01:37.141
Tesla Roddy notes that gold tinted glass is modeled on space suit visors.

00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:42.781
Titanium accents are carried over from rocket hardware and appear on both the car and the rocket fleet.

00:01:43.281 --> 00:01:47.001
The paint choice aligns the Roadster with SpaceX vehicle protection needs.

00:01:47.001 --> 00:01:53.456
A Florida homeowner paid $60,000 for a Tesla Solar Plus Powerwall setup that was installed

00:01:53.456 --> 00:01:55.516
for backup, Yahoo Tech Reports.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:59.216
The system did not engage when the grid went down during a hurricane.

00:01:59.836 --> 00:02:04.116
The homeowner had expected the panels and powerwall to keep electricity on through an extended

00:02:04.116 --> 00:02:04.656
outage.

00:02:05.216 --> 00:02:10.096
Obrus powertrain and Obrus technologies have filed for insolvency with combined debts

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:13.296
electric puts at roughly 31.8 million euros.

00:02:13.296 --> 00:02:18.596
The Austrian firm spent more than a decade developing its hyperhybrid range extender system

00:02:18.596 --> 00:02:21.236
for Tesla vehicles and never reach production.

00:02:21.756 --> 00:02:23.696
Three group companies are now insolvent.

00:02:24.256 --> 00:02:28.976
The powertrain unit owes about 18.85 million euros to 34 creditors.

00:02:29.276 --> 00:02:34.736
The patent-holding unit owes 6.08 million euros, and the German sales arm added another

00:02:34.736 --> 00:02:37.076
6.8 million euros in liabilities.

00:02:37.076 --> 00:02:37.236
securities.

00:02:37.616 --> 00:02:42.716
Founder Frank Oberst cited high development costs, failed investor talks, and Europe's

00:02:42.716 --> 00:02:44.616
shift to full battery electric vehicles.

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:50.269
Robotaxi remote takeovers have produced five crashes in National Highway Traffic Safety

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:53.049
Administration, or NHTSA reports.

00:02:53.829 --> 00:02:56.309
Electric says every instance ended in contact.

00:02:56.929 --> 00:03:02.729
Two new August incidents in Dallas and Austin involved a model-wise striking an SUV at 0.4

00:03:02.729 --> 00:03:08.049
miles per hour, and a dumpster at one mile per hour while under remote control. Both were

00:03:08.049 --> 00:03:13.169
low-speed property damage events with no passengers aboard. The remote operator field in the

00:03:13.169 --> 00:03:20.063
reports is coded as remote, commercial, or test. Electric reports the 68-year-old SUV driver was

00:03:20.063 --> 00:03:27.563
killed. Tesla's report to NHTSA marked autopilot and full-self driving, or FSD, as verified engaged.

00:03:28.043 --> 00:03:31.723
The report lists the New Jersey State Police as the investigating agency,

00:03:31.723 --> 00:03:34.663
and notes the information came from media sources.

00:03:35.103 --> 00:03:36.943
Fields describing the vehicle's actions

00:03:36.943 --> 00:03:39.083
and software version remain redacted.

00:03:39.984 --> 00:03:43.064
Jody Kerns, senior manager of CyberCab General Assembly

00:03:43.064 --> 00:03:45.604
at Gigatexis, is moving to Rivian

00:03:45.604 --> 00:03:47.164
as director of General Assembly

00:03:47.164 --> 00:03:49.404
for the R2 program in Normal Illinois.

00:03:50.124 --> 00:03:52.324
Electric reports he had run final assembly

00:03:52.324 --> 00:03:55.104
on the CyberCab from its first steering wheelless unit

00:03:55.104 --> 00:03:57.524
through the start of commercial service in Austin.

00:03:58.264 --> 00:04:01.364
Kerns previously spent 14 years at Volkswagen of America,

00:04:01.364 --> 00:04:06.124
ending as director of assembly. He also spent four years in Toyota paint shops.

00:04:06.684 --> 00:04:11.547
This is the second CyberCab launch leader to leave Tesla this year. The official

00:04:11.547 --> 00:04:17.407
Tesla account posted a 0-60 time of 0.81 seconds alongside video of the vehicle

00:04:17.407 --> 00:04:22.227
accelerating. A follow-up post clarified 0.67 seconds with rollout

00:04:22.227 --> 00:04:26.267
subtracted. Those times applied to the highest performance variant shown in

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:31.067
the Texas demonstration. Reservations are now open on the Tesla Motors subreddit for

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.307
performance, thrust, and rocket versions.

00:04:33.827 --> 00:04:35.727
Thrust is limited to one per customer.

00:04:36.287 --> 00:04:38.367
Rocket is available by invitation only.

00:04:38.847 --> 00:04:44.587
Thrust requires a $5,000 deposit and the remaining $245,000 within 10 days.

00:04:45.167 --> 00:04:47.527
The performance model is described as road ready.

00:04:48.585 --> 00:04:53.305
Lars Moravie described an underbody fan suction system that pulls the car toward the surface

00:04:53.305 --> 00:04:55.305
to enable inverted driving on the ramp.

00:04:56.045 --> 00:04:59.285
EuroNews reports the system is rated for up to 2G of force.

00:04:59.285 --> 00:05:04.685
course. Remaining propulsion after the suction phase borrows from SpaceX, Musk noted the

00:05:04.685 --> 00:05:10.369
car can perform roles and gymnastics but is not necessarily safety optimized. The base

00:05:10.369 --> 00:05:16.169
performance Roadster carries no thrusters, inside EVs reports. The rocket variance thrusters

00:05:16.169 --> 00:05:21.389
are specified for vertical and rotational movement. Car and driver posted exterior photos

00:05:21.389 --> 00:05:25.929
of the new Roadster showing the updated design language. The gallery highlights hidden

00:05:25.929 --> 00:05:30.649
headlights and a full-length tail light. The roadster leaped over Tesla's entire lineup

00:05:30.649 --> 00:05:36.709
during the demonstration, inside EVs reports. That lineup included a semi-standing 13.5

00:05:36.709 --> 00:05:42.467
feet tall. Carrying compressed gas as a permanent passenger is a mass problem before it is a

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:47.847
stunt problem. That propellant load has to ride along at all times, even on a trip where the

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:52.967
nozzles never fire. It subtracts from the range claim and adds structural mass the seats and

00:05:52.967 --> 00:05:55.147
light weight materials are already trying to offset.

00:05:55.847 --> 00:06:00.607
Filling it again after use needs an onboard compressor or a refueling step, and that

00:06:00.607 --> 00:06:04.107
adds support system complexity a street car does not usually carry.

00:06:04.747 --> 00:06:07.467
The demonstration load may differ across the three variants.

00:06:08.087 --> 00:06:11.927
Suction under the car is being used instead of conventional wings or splitters.

00:06:12.447 --> 00:06:16.667
Fans can pull the body down without the extra high-speed drag of those arrow surfaces.

00:06:17.187 --> 00:06:21.347
They also need continuous electrical power, and the moving parts have to survive road

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:26.227
debris and weather. Taking that force onto variable road surfaces and through regulatory

00:06:26.227 --> 00:06:32.427
crash standards is a set of variables the prototype has not addressed in public testing. Fan-powered

00:06:32.427 --> 00:06:37.347
draw competes with the propulsion and battery systems already tasked with sub-1-second sprints.

00:06:37.967 --> 00:06:42.527
Repeated operation without external support remains unproven outside the Texas event.

00:06:43.187 --> 00:06:47.987
A thruster pack size for a one-seat rocket variant may prove oversized or undersized

00:06:47.987 --> 00:06:51.287
on a two-seat performance model or on a commercial semi.

00:06:51.967 --> 00:06:56.527
Amortizing that hardware only lowers per unit cost if it meets the strictest requirements

00:06:56.527 --> 00:06:58.787
of every program without heavy redesign.

00:06:59.607 --> 00:07:04.807
Roadster production timing overlaps expected volume ramps on the other programs, which tightens

00:07:04.807 --> 00:07:06.787
the window for variant specific changes.

00:07:07.287 --> 00:07:11.847
A single component failure or a regulatory delay can then hit multiple revenue streams

00:07:11.847 --> 00:07:12.427
at once.

00:07:12.427 --> 00:07:17.987
Before we go, any additional remote takeover contacts would surface in the next NHTSA

00:07:17.987 --> 00:07:18.527
filings.

00:07:18.927 --> 00:07:21.027
And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news.

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:29.347
TSLA closed at $362.44, down $4.72 or 1.3%.

